  "rationale": "No single non-foothold step is a single point of failure, because the target has several independent routes. crownData:exfiltrate is an OR over shareMount, dbReplica, vaultRead and codeRepo. (1) fileServer is reachable via sshKey (from exposedApi), via ssoLogin (iotDevice from phishing AND workstation from wifiGuest/phishing), or via vpnSession (tokenCache from supplychain AND ciRunner from exposedApi/wifiGuest). fileServer then gives shareMount and dbReplica. (2) backupHost comes from apiToken (dmzWeb from vpnGateway AND memoryDump from supplychain/workstation) and gives shareMount and dbReplica. (3) monitoringHost comes from browserStore (wifiGuest/ciRunner) or sshKey and gives codeRepo. (4) hypervisor comes from dbLogin AND printServer and gives shareMount and vaultRead. Blocking any one step leaves at least one route: blocking fileServer leaves backupHost and monitoringHost; blocking sshKey leaves fileServer via ssoLogin or vpnSession; blocking memoryDump leaves the fileServer route; blocking shareMount, dbReplica, vaultRead or codeRepo leaves the other collection steps."
